    },
    "Four hexadecimal digits, for example 0x2704." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vier hexadezimale Stellen, zum Beispiel 0x2704."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Four hexadecimal digits, for example 0x2704."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Leave this as it is. A computer reads two numbers when something is plugged in: who built it, and which product it is. This is the second one. It changes nothing about how the box sounds or behaves, and the Sound Settings show the product name above, not this number. Give a second board a different one only when a program has to tell the two apart." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lass das so. Ein Rechner liest beim Anstecken zwei Zahlen: wer das Gerät gebaut hat und welches Produkt es ist. Das hier ist die zweite. Sie ändert nichts am Klang und am Verhalten der Box, und in den Toneinstellungen steht der Gerätename von oben, nicht diese Zahl. Ein zweites Board bekommt nur dann eine andere, wenn ein Programm die beiden auseinanderhalten muss."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Leave this as it is. A computer reads two numbers when something is plugged in: who built it, and which product it is. This is the second one. It changes nothing about how the box sounds or behaves, and the Sound Settings show the product name above, not this number. Give a second board a different one only when a program has to tell the two apart."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Leave this as it is. It is the number a host reads beside the vendor, and the Sound Settings show the product name above rather than this. Give a second board its own only when a program has to tell the two apart." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the product ID field.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
